                <pb facs="0251" n="241" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg241"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.5151/674: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-05-12T17:00:00-04:00">May 12, 1937—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>37. Your 67, May 10, 4 p.m. Although the Department does not consider it
                    advisable to proceed at this time as suggested in your telegram, please continue
                    your oral representations to the appropriate Argentine authorities along the
                    lines set forth in the Embassy’s note of February 3 and the Department’s
                    telegram No. 34, of April 24, 1937. Please continue to telegraph important
                    developments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
